# malachite Wi-Fi monitor mode + injection — SELinux
#
# Deliberately minimal. Do NOT blanket `setenforce 0` (the o1s module did, and
# it is the wrong approach — it masks real denials and weakens the whole system).
#
# The correct rules can only be written from the ACTUAL AVC denials seen when a
# tester arms monitor and runs the native tools with SELinux enforcing. Capture
# them with:  dmesg | grep avc   (or `logcat -b events | grep avc`)
# then add targeted allow rules here for the exact domain/type/class/perm.
#
# Likely domains to watch: the shell/ksu domain running iw/ip and the aircrack
# tools, operating on the wlan netdev and the driver's char/proc nodes. Add
# rules only for what is actually denied; keep SELinux enforcing.
#
# (no rules yet — fill from on-device AVCs)
